he cited shift without overstating causation."},{"excerpt":"Dat maakt de relatie tussen wolven en elanden geen verhaal van één roofdier dat alles bepaalt.","claim":"The wolf–elk relationship should not be understood as one predator determining everything.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Consequently, changes in prey selection and kill rates through time result from complex interactions among these factors.","narrative":"niet bij wolven als enige bepalende kracht","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This is a fair summary of the source's account of interacting factors rather than a claim that wolves alone determine outcomes.","materiality":"Moderate; it frames the central interpretation and guards against a single-cause account."},{"excerpt":"Andere roofdieren, het beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer spelen eveneens mee in veranderingen in predatie en de effecten daarvan op elanden.","claim":"Other predators, ungulate management outside the park, and weather contribute to changes in wolf predation and its effects on elk.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Changes in wolf predation patterns and impacts on prey species like elk are inextricably linked to other factors, such as other predators, management of ungulates outside the park, and weather","narrative":"veranderingen in predatie en de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source names these factors and links them to predation patterns and impacts on elk. “Spelen mee” does not claim that their relative contributions are quantified.","materiality":"High; it summarizes the source's explanation of interacting influences."},{"excerpt":"Wolven zijn onderdeel van een breder samenspel: sociale groepen, voedselrelaties en predatiepatronen die veranderen met de omstandigheden.","claim":"Wolves are part of a broader ecological interplay involving social groups, food relationships, and predation patterns that change with circumstances.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The pack is a complex social family","narrative":"wolven maken deel uit van sociale en voedselrelaties, terwijl veranderingen in predatie en de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This concluding synthesis is consistent with the source's descriptions of pack sociality, animals benefiting from kills, and predation changing amid interacting factors.","materiality":"Moderate; it summarizes the piece's central theme without adding a specific unsupported ecosystem effect."}]}

